    "reasoning": "All 16 selected answers are mathematically correct and supported by their own captured worked solutions. q-79799: I and III are constant multiples of the given solutions; II contains e^{-4t}, whose characteristic value is 24 rather than 0. q-131032: the selected function is the linear combination (2/3)e^x-(1/3)e^{-2x}. q-106929: x^2+x and -x^2 both have degree 2, but their sum x does not, so addition is not closed. q-94798: multiplying the rational-coefficient polynomial x by the real scalar sqrt(2) produces an irrational coefficient. q-106938: A3 removes the additive zero, then A2 reassociates the sum. q-35559: A7 distributes scalar addition, and A3 removes the additive zero. q-162901: independence gives P(Y=-1)=0.03/0.1=0.3. q-110385: independence gives f(3,1)=0.5(0.25)=0.125. q-142874: (1/2)/(1/4+1/2)=2/3. q-142876: 0.1/(0.25+0.1)=2/7, rounding to 0.29. q-142899: (0.1+0)/(0.25+0.05+0.1+0)=0.25. q-142906: (1/18+0+1/6)/(1/9+1/18+0+1/6)=2/3; its initial worked formula omits the P symbol on the left. q-142902: (1/9)/(5/27+1/9)=3/8. q-114424: 0.2/(0.3+0.2+0.1)=1/3, rounding to 0.33. q-142915: dividing the Y=4 column by its total 0.25 gives 0.4, 0.6, 0. Its worked solution incorrectly writes P(Y=1) in an intermediate denominator; the correct denominator is P(Y=4). q-142928: dividing the X=0 row by its total 0.5 gives 0.4, 0.2, 0.4. Its worked solution incorrectly labels the other row X=1 instead of X=2, introduces f_{X|Y} instead of f_{Y|X}, and reverses the conditional events in the three intermediate probability labels. These authored source errors do not change either final table. No selected answer disagrees with MA's stated final answer. No earlier submission or grade was provided.",
